# Kaopiz Mobile Development Checklist

## High Priority Rules

1. Automatic Error Logging
- Implement automatic error logging for all exceptions and crashes
- Log important debugging information including:
  - Stack trace
  - User actions that led to the error
  - Device information and OS version
  - App state
- Use proper logging levels (debug, info, warning, error)
- Implement proper crash reporting tools (e.g., Firebase Crashlytics)

2. UI/UX Interaction Standards
- Ensure all interactive elements are easily tappable
- Maintain minimum touch target size of 48x48 pixels
- Implement proper padding for icon buttons
- Follow Material Design guidelines for spacing and touch areas
- Ensure proper contrast ratios and visibility

3. Testing Requirements
- Perform thorough testing on actual devices
- Test on both iOS and Android platforms
- Verify functionality in different network conditions
- Document test results in JIRA

4. Requirements Compliance
- Ensure implementation matches design specifications
- Follow documented user flows
- Validate against acceptance criteria
- Document any deviations or assumptions

5. Null Safety and Exception Handling
- Implement proper null safety checks
- Handle all possible error states
- Show appropriate error messages to users
- Implement graceful fallbacks

6. Data Consistency
- Implement proper local database transactions
- Implement proper state management
- Handle offline/online synchronization
- Implement proper data rollback mechanisms for local storage
- Handle app termination and state restoration

7. API Request Optimization
- Implement proper request timeout handling
- Handle API errors gracefully
- Implement retry mechanisms for failed requests
- Optimize for mobile network conditions
- Implement proper request caching
- Handle low bandwidth scenarios

8. UI Interaction Protection
- Prevent multiple taps on buttons during processing
- Show loading indicators for async operations
- Implement proper state management for UI elements
- Re-enable interactions after operation completion

9. Change Impact Documentation
- Document impact scope in JIRA
- Note affected screens and features
- Document API changes and their impact
- List potential side effects

10. Security - Environment Variables
- Use .env files for sensitive configuration
- Never commit API keys to source control
- Use proper key management for different environments
- Implement secure storage for sensitive data

11. Authentication
- Implement proper token-based authentication
- Validate all API requests
- Handle session expiration
- Implement secure biometric authentication when required

12. Secure Data Transmission
- Use HTTPS for all network requests
- Implement certificate pinning
- Encrypt sensitive data in transit
- Use secure websocket connections when needed

13. Sensitive Data Storage
- Use secure storage for sensitive user data
- Implement proper encryption for local storage
- Clear sensitive data on logout
- Follow platform-specific security guidelines

14. Data Privacy
- Minimize collection of personal information
- Implement proper data masking
- Follow GDPR/CCPA guidelines where applicable
- Implement proper data deletion mechanisms

## Medium Priority Rules

15. Architecture Compliance
- Follow clean architecture principles
- Maintain proper separation of concerns
- Use proper dependency injection
- Follow established project patterns

16. Code Documentation
- Document complex business logic
- Add comments for non-obvious implementations
- Document widget parameters
- Include example usage in comments

17. Code Reusability
- Create reusable widgets
- Implement proper abstraction layers
- Use proper inheritance and composition
- Maintain DRY principles

18. Version Control
- Use proper JIRA references in commits
- Follow branch naming conventions
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Create proper pull request documentation

19. Edge Cases
- Document special conditions
- Handle rare but possible scenarios
- Implement proper error states
- Test edge cases thoroughly

20. Conditional Logic
- Document complex conditions
- Implement proper else cases
- Handle all possible states
- Use switch statements for multiple conditions

21. Concurrency
- Handle async operations properly
- Implement proper state management
- Handle race conditions
- Use proper isolates for heavy computations

22. Scalability
- Implement proper caching mechanisms
- Handle mobile memory constraints
- Optimize for different screen sizes and orientations
- Support different device capabilities
- Handle low-end device performance
- Implement proper image scaling and caching

23. Performance Optimization
- Avoid nested loops
- Implement proper list virtualization
- Use const constructors
- Implement proper image caching

24. Query Optimization
- Implement proper pagination for mobile views
- Use efficient local database queries
- Cache query results appropriately
- Optimize data fetching for mobile networks
- Implement proper offline data access

25. Dependencies
- Use trusted packages only
- Keep dependencies up to date
- Document dependency purposes
- Check license compliance

26. Third-party Integration
- Follow integration guidelines
- Implement proper error handling
- Document integration requirements
- Maintain vendor documentation

27. Notifications
- Implement proper notification channels
- Handle notification permissions
- Implement proper deep linking
- Handle notification actions

28. Testing Environment
- Use proper mobile test data
- Test on real mobile devices
- Document mobile-specific test scenarios
- Implement proper mocking for mobile components
- Test on different OS versions and screen sizes

29. Data Security
- Use proper encryption algorithms
- Implement secure key storage
- Follow platform security guidelines
- Implement proper certificate handling

## Low Priority Rules

30. Code Formatting
- Follow Flutter style guide
- Maintain consistent formatting
- Use proper indentation
- Follow naming conventions

31. Code Length
- Keep methods short and focused
- Limit file length
- Maintain proper widget structure
- Break down complex widgets

32. Code Cleanliness
- Remove unused code
- Clean up comments
- Remove debug prints
- Remove unused imports

33. Performance Metrics
- Monitor app startup time
- Track frame rendering time
- Monitor memory usage
- Track battery consumption
- Monitor app size
- Track mobile network usage

34. Code Complexity
- Limit conditional nesting
- Use proper design patterns
- Break down complex logic
- Implement proper abstractions

35. Resource Optimization
- Optimize mobile asset usage
- Implement proper image resolution for different devices
- Handle mobile memory efficiently
- Clean up resources properly
- Optimize app bundle size
- Implement proper asset caching

36. Authentication Timeout
- Implement proper session management
- Handle token refresh
- Implement proper logout
- Handle background state

37. Social Authentication
- Follow platform guidelines
- Implement proper error handling
- Handle cancellation properly
- Maintain session state

38. Debug Information
- Remove debug prints in release
- Handle logging properly
- Implement proper error reporting
- Clean up development artifacts

39. Cache Management
- Implement proper cache invalidation
- Handle cache size limits
- Clean up old cache data
- Implement proper cache strategies

These rules are mandatory for all Kaopiz mobile development projects and will be automatically enforced during code review. Each rule should be checked and validated before submitting code for review. 